<description>
Move each scattered color into the rectangular frame whose interior checkerboard has the same cell count.

Input structure:
- The background is the most common color.
- Foreground contains one or more one-cell-thick rectangular frames.
- All non-frame foreground pixels are isolated markers grouped by color.

Rule:
- For each frame, count the cells of the checkerboard pattern inside its border,
  starting at the upper-left interior cell.
- Match that frame to the unique outside marker color with the same number of pixels.
- Erase all outside markers and paint the matched color into the frame interior's
  upper-left-starting checkerboard cells.

Key insight:
- The scattered pixels are not placed by their coordinates; their color populations
  are counts that select which frame interior they should fill.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "outside monochromatic marker mask s",
  "dst": "hollow rectangular frame interior d",
  "match_cond": "|s| == number of upper-left-starting checkerboard cells in d",
  "transform": "erase s from original cells and fill those checkerboard cells of d with s.color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
task_id: df8cc377
type: move_to_match

spec:
  grid: 12-22 rows x 20-26 cols, background 0
  frames:
    count: 2-3 rectangular hollow frames, each a 1-cell-thick border ring
    outer_size: 3-8 rows x 3-11 cols (interior 1-6 x 1-9)
    each frame has a unique color; no frame touches the grid edge (margin >= 1)
    frames do not overlap; interiors are empty (background)
  markers:
    count: same as frame count; each marker group is a distinct color
    marker colors are disjoint from frame colors
    all markers are isolated single pixels scattered on the background
    no marker falls inside any frame's bounding box
  matching: |
    checkerboard capacity of frame interior = ceil(ih * iw / 2) where (ih, iw) is interior size
    each marker color's pixel count == exactly one frame's capacity (bijection)
    all capacities are distinct across frames
  output: |
    erase all markers; fill each frame's interior with its matched marker color
    in a checkerboard starting at upper-left interior cell: (r-r0-1 + c-c0-1) % 2 == 0

generation_strategy: output-first
  1. Pick grid size in range. Pick N=2-3 frames.
  2. For each frame choose interior (ih, iw) with ih in [1,6], iw in [1,9] ensuring
     all checkerboard capacities ceil(ih*iw/2) are distinct.
  3. Assign N unique colors to frames and N different unique colors to markers (all 2N distinct).
  4. Place frames on grid with margin >= 1 from edges and no overlap (including borders).
  5. Fill each frame interior with its matched marker color in checkerboard pattern -> output.
  6. To build input: clear interiors back to background, scatter each marker color as
     isolated single pixels (count = capacity) on background cells outside all frame bboxes.
```
</generation_spec>
